<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="103" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Approval: eligible approvers, worklist, approve</title>
    <phase>4 Review and approval (WP4) — wave W4-2</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Decides who may approve payment of an invoice (authorization) and freezes the approved total; a wrong resolution lets a non-eligible user approve or hides an invoice from its approvers.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Cross-cutting design: approver resolution from role choices and assignment fields, re-resolution without a change event, I-2 with the open F-2 question, idempotent Decision Record and lifecycle sequencing.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P4-B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>100, 021, 024, 025, 074</deps>
    <tags>bff, api, auth, signals</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Resolve eligible approvers for an invoice from its core record's sprk_billingapproverrole (empty = the settings default for the core type), keep them current on the approval portion so the "Invoices to review" view lists the invoice for each of them, and add the approve operation: any one eligible approver approves (I-2 enforced), status moves to Approved through 014, the approved total is frozen on the portion, and exactly one Decision Record names who decided.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in authorization design, Dataverse relationships and idempotent multi-step writes.</role>

  <goal>EligibleApproverResolver, InvoiceApprovalService and InvoiceApprovalEndpoints.cs (GET approval state, POST approve), a refresh path for eligible approvers, and tests including a seeding proof that a non-eligible caller gets 403.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-35 (acceptance: non-eligible user 403; approve with a Flagged line refused; second approval after the first is a no-op), FR-11 (eligible approvers resolved at acceptance and re-resolved when assignment fields or the role field change before a decision), FR-14 (empty role = settings default; test per core type), I-2, FR-30, D-33 / D-40 / D-54, spec Assumptions (re-resolution event-driven with a recheck when an approver opens the invoice). 024: global choice options map to assignment fields (Assigned Attorney 1 / 2, Assigned Paralegal 1 / 2, Assigned To Internal, Assigned To External, Assigned To); exact column names in 024's notes. 021: sprk_invoiceapproval (sprk_approvalstatus, sprk_approvedamount, sprk_eligibleresolvedon, sprk_decidedby → contact, sprk_decidedon, sprk_decisionrecord) and N:N sprk_invoiceapproval_eligibleapprover_contact; assignment fields target contact; contact.sprk_systemuser links to the user. 025: IEbillingSettingsReader default approver roles per core type. Caller identity: Services/Identity/SystemUserIdentityResolver.cs:33 (ResolveSystemUserIdAsync from the token oid). Lifecycle: 014 (Transitioned / AlreadyInTarget / Refused). Decision Record: 074's recorder (approve action). Correction rows: 027. The "Invoices to review" view is built by 029 on the N:N. No Dataverse change event for assignment fields exists in the BFF (grep finds none); scheduled-job precedent: Services/Access/SecureChildReconciliationJob.cs:85, registered with AddScheduledJob at Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs:643.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/EligibleApproverResolver.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/InvoiceApprovalService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/EligibleApproverRefreshJob.cs (IScheduledJob; see escalation)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/InvoiceApprovalEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">049's approval-portion creation (file named in 049's notes): one call to the resolver at acceptance — treat as a shared append point</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/FinanceModule.cs (shared append point)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs:376-377 (shared append point)</file>
