  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Read 021, 024, 025 and 074 notes; resolve the F-2 and refresh escalations below before coding the approve route.</step>
    <step order="1">EligibleApproverResolver: invoice → core record (type, id) → role values or settings default → assignment-field contacts → systemusers; returns contacts, users, display names; also writes the N:N diff and sprk_eligibleresolvedon (add / remove only what changed).</step>
    <step order="2">Wire the resolver into 049's approval-portion creation (acceptance time), into GET approval (recheck on open) and into the refresh job.</step>
    <step order="3">GET /api/finance/invoices/{invoiceId}/approval: eligible approver names, canApprove (caller eligible and I-2 satisfied), open-line counts, status, decided by / on. 104 reuses the same eligibility for reject / return.</step>
    <step order="4">POST .../approve (decision id): eligibility, I-2, F-2 handling of undecided Clean lines, 014 transition, portion update, 074 record — in an order that keeps exactly-once semantics.</step>
    <step order="5">Verify in dev that 029's "Invoices to review" view lists the invoice for each eligible approver and not for another user; record evidence.</step>
    <step order="6">Tests: resolver per core type with role set and with empty role (settings default); contact without user ignored; approve happy path; Flagged / Pending refused; non-eligible 403; second approve no-op; retry after partial failure writes one record; contract tests 401 / 403 / disabled.</step>
    <step order="7">Seeding proof (non-eligible approver guard): remove the service eligibility check, show the 403 test fails, restore; record in notes.</step>
    <step order="8">dotnet build and dotnet test green; publish-size delta and vulnerable-package check recorded.</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to "✅ [done]".</step>
    <step order="10">Record deviations (F-2 answer, refresh cadence, D-64 finalisation rule) in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Owner decided D-72 (F-2): approve is allowed with undecided Clean lines; it sets them Accepted and writes Accepted in bulk correction rows (islabel false), and any AI-sourced field of an individually decided line with no correction row gets Unreviewed.</trigger>
    <trigger>Owner decided D-78: live check at approve (mandatory) and recheck on GET, plus either EligibleApproverRefreshJob over In Review portions (cadence in notes, e.g. 15 minutes) or the lower-overhead alternative (a stale flag plus a manual refresh action); choose one and record which and why. Event-driven re-resolution is out (it would need a Dataverse-side trigger, ADR-002).</trigger>
    <trigger>If 049's file must be edited and 105 has an uncommitted change in it, re-read and add only this task's call; if the change cannot be a single call, STOP and coordinate.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Spec section 11 row "sprk_invoiceapproval" (021) and "Review / approval / export / rule endpoints"; grep finds no approver resolution from sprk_billingapproverrole and no approve route; Signals Decision Record gate fields hold history, not pending eligibility.</existing>
    <extension>Resolver and service are new because no service reads approver roles; endpoints in their own file (P4-B no overlap); the refresh job uses the existing ADR-036 host rather than a new mechanism.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>No invoice can be approved, eligible approvers never see it in their view, and FR-11, FR-14, FR-35 and success criterion 4 fail.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build, test</tool>
    <tool name="dataverse MCP / Web API">dev evidence for the view</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">Services/Finance/EligibleApproverResolver.cs; InvoiceApprovalService.cs; EligibleApproverRefreshJob.cs; Api/Finance/InvoiceApprovalEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="test">EligibleApproverResolverTests.cs; InvoiceApprovalServiceTests.cs; InvoiceApprovalEndpointsAuthorizationContractTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Routes return 401 unauthenticated, 503 ebilling.disabled when off; approve returns 403 ebilling.approver.not_eligible for a caller with invoice access who is not eligible; seeding proof recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">For each core type, a record with roles set resolves the users in the selected assignment fields; a record with an empty role resolves the settings default for its type.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Approve with a Flagged or Pending line is 409 with counts; with none, the invoice becomes Approved, the portion stores approved amount, decider and time, and one Decision Record names the approver.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A second approve (same or another eligible approver) is a no-op with no new Decision Record; a retry after a failure between transition and record yields exactly one record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Changing a core record's assignment field before a decision changes the stored eligible approvers on the next refresh or GET, and the approve check uses the live value immediately.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Dev evidence: the "Invoices to review" view shows the invoice for each eligible approver and not for a non-eligible user.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build 0 errors; all tests green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta measured against a fresh master build and recorded in task notes; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Parallel group P4-B: own files, except shared append points FinanceModule.cs, EndpointMappingExtensions.cs and 049's portion-creation file (105 may also touch 049 — re-read immediately before editing; run /conflict-check before the PR). In-app approver notification is completed by 132 from the stored approvers; no notification code here. The refresh job may need a sprk_backgroundjob row in dev; 112 seeds it.</notes>

